    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ccb0ee0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">s</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You follow the path through the trees. As you do you realise that you are flanked either side by the kingfisher and goldcrest from before. They fly on ahead of you as the trees open out into a clearing.

Shepherd&apos;s Hut
You can see Ottelie here.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>YES</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ccb43d0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to old man</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can say anything, the Old Man waves his hand and says &quot;Listen, we do not have much time. I can help you, but in exchange you must remind me of things forgotten.&quot; You stare back at him, more than a little confused. He continues, &quot;My memory is not all it once was. I was instructed to hold onto bits of information in preparation for the day you arrived, but in order to do so I needed to remove some of my own memories. Oh don&apos;t worry, I made some notes so that I could remind myself when the time came. I made three cards. Not here. In another place. You know what I mean. On the back of each are clues to the memories I gave up. Well, I mean the memories are probably still in here.&quot; The old man taps the side of his head, smiling. &quot;I just need to hear a specific word to reactivate them. That&apos;s where you come in. Help me regain my memories and in return I will give you the information you need.&quot;

&gt;</result>
