  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ccc5190">
    <command xml:space="preserve">tell the old man about Ophiuchus</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The old man&apos;s face turns serious, as if remembering something of great import. &quot;I remember now. I remember when we defeated the Servants of the Black Dawn. Seems so long ago now. What a wonderful night that was... But anyway, here&apos;s the knowledge you need: Page 87.&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ccc88e0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">help</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In this game you can explore an alternate dimension. There are many things to see and there may well be people or animals you can interact with. You can interact with the game by typing simple commands, for example:

&quot;look at the oak tree&quot;
&quot;take the book.&quot;
&quot;open the chest.&quot;
&quot;unlock the door with the brass key&quot;

To move between scenes type the letter corresponding to the compass directions (n, ne, e, se, s, sw, w, nw), as well as &quot;in&quot; and &quot;out&quot;. The description of each room will usually give you hints as to where you can go. If you want to get a description of a room you are in, simply type &quot;look&quot;. Often the place descriptions will change depending on your actions, giving you clues on how to proceed.

A non-exhaustive list of commands you may use: look; read; talk; say; tell; whisper;listen; unlock; take; open; close; push; press. You may be surprised to see there is no &quot;use&quot; command; the word is a little bit too generic to work well with the game&apos;s parser.

If you get stuck and the room description doesn&apos;t clue you in, type &quot;hint&quot;. This will give you a clue as to what you&apos;re supposed to be doing (if anything) in your current location. It could be that the answer to a particular puzzle exists in the real world rather than in-game. If you&apos;re STILL stuck, you could try asking a wise and knowledgable man for a clue...

Some important commands are &quot;save&quot; and &quot;restore&quot;, which do exactly what you would expect, allowing you to maintain progress between sessions. Oh and &quot;help&quot; will display this help text.

Good luck. Have fun. Don&apos;t die (don&apos;t worry, you can&apos;t die in this game).

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ccc8c30"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ccc8c30">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">In-Between
You are.. somewhere. Swirling mists curl out of the blackness that appears to exist in between your world and some other place, just out of reach. You hear a faint sound, but you&apos;ll have to actively listen to make sense of it.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
