  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd3a4c0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">e</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">
Ozymandias
Two vast and trunkless legs of stone stand in the desert. Near them on the sand, half sunk, a shattered visage lies. The legs are atop a pedestal. &quot;Vast&quot; is an understatement as well. Each mighty leg must be at least two metres tall. Just looking up at them makes you feel slightly dizzy.

You can see a weasel here.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd3d930"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd3d930">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x visage</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A shattered visage, whose frown, and wrinkled lip, and sneer of cold command, tell that its sculptor well those passions read which yet survive, stamped on these lifeless things, the hand that mocked them, and the heart that fed.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd40e60"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd40e60">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x weaset</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You can&apos;t see any such thing.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd442e0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd442e0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">oops weasel</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A timid yet adorable mustelid scurries too and fro amongst the scattered stones. When she notices you she gives an excited yip and climbs up to the top of the pedestal and... speaks? &quot;Claire! come closer and talk to me. I don&apos;t have long.&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd47af0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd47af0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x weasel</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A timid yet adorable mustelid sits atop the pedestal with an urgent look on her face.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd4b490"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd4b490">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to weasel</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The weasel looks at you excitedly, before saying &quot;Claire, thank you for finding me. Do you recognise me? I am Ottelie. Oh Claire, don&apos;t act so surprised. I know I might look strange in my weasel form, but it was the only way I could escape the cage I&apos;m trapped in.

&quot;Look, it&apos;s too complicated to explain and I don&apos;t have time. My magic can only last so long before I have to return to my body. I need you to come to the Dusklight Forest. That&apos;s where I am imprisoned. I know you have the kingfisher&apos;s feather.

&quot;What&apos;s that? You don&apos;t have all of the map? Oh that will never do... OK listen. You must visit the Old man of the Mountain, but there&apos;s a terrible spell making the weather in the Skypeak Mountains absolutely inhospitable. Find a way to get into the Arena of Champions, back up there to the west. Speak to the Shades of the Heroes. They might be able to help.&quot;

Ottelie the weasel starts to flicker and fade before your very eyes.

&quot;Oh no! I think my magic is running out! Look to my companions! They led you here, they will lead you out!

&quot;Help me Claire! I believe in you!&quot;

As the weasel fades from view, you hear the cry of birds from above.

&quot;Kew-ahhh! Kew-ahhh!&quot;

You recognise the call of the Kingfisher and look up. Now only is the magnificent blue bird circling above you, but it is joined with a smaller bird, a tiny goldcrest. As you watch, they settle on top of the mighty legs of the ruined statue, the Kingfisher on the left leg, the goldfinch on the right.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd4aeb0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd4aeb0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at the pedestal</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">On the pedestal these words appear: &quot;My name is Ozymandias, king of kings: Look on my works, ye Mighty, and despair!&quot; Underneath the plaque sits what appears to be a control panel. You don&apos;t remember Shelley writing about this.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cd524c0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cd524c0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at panel</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A small control panel with a row of four buttons and LEDs above them. The LEDs currently look like this:

