  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c991b30">
    <command xml:space="preserve">push button 1</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You push Button 1. Instantly, LED 1 changes from green to blue.
You hear a tremendous sound to the west, the metallic grind of iron on stone. The birds atop the legs let out a satisfied cry and fly away.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c995040"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c995040">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Ozymandias
Two vast and trunkless legs of stone stand in the desert. Near them on the sand, half sunk, a shattered visage lies. The legs are atop a pedestal. &quot;Vast&quot; is an understatement as well. Each mighty leg must be at least two metres tall. Just looking up at them makes you feel slightly dizzy.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c9985a0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c9985a0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at legs</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Vast stone legs extend upwards, but whatever torso once existed atop them is long gone now, obliterated by the cruel passage of endless ages. Atop the left leg, resplendent in its glory, sits the kingfisher. Atop the right leg, tiny but audacious, sits the goldcrest.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c99bc30"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c99bc30">
    <command xml:space="preserve">w</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">
Desert ruins
You find yourself in the midst of an arid desert, sand stretching all around you and continuing off towards the shimmering horizon while the relentless sun beats down upon you. After a while you become acutely aware of the lack of water and inwardly hope that you don&apos;t have to spend too long here.

Some distance to the east is a stone ruin of some sort. It&apos;s difficult to make out from here.

Ahead of you to the north is the crumbling edifice of a once mighty fortress. The huge rusted iron doors now stand ajar, allowing access into the ruins.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c99f400"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c99f400">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at doors</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Vast and unyielding and impossibly ancient, you wonder who could have built this enormous portal. The doors must weigh hundreds of tons; they are covered in thick red rust but you detect no signs of corrosion or structural weakness. They stand open before you.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c9a2b90"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316c9a2b90">
    <command xml:space="preserve">n</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">You head through the huge iron doors into the tunnel beyond. Eventually the tunnel opens out into what appears to be an arena.

Arena of Champions
You stand inside a vast arena, and for a brief moment experience a vision of an ancient time, the stalls filled with thousands of people cheering on the mighty warriors who clashed on the sands. A rush of adrenaline fills you, the exuberance of the fight making your heart beat faster. As suddenly as it appeared, the vision fades, and the stalls lie empty, filling the arena with an unsettling silence. A plinth of alabaster occupies the centre of the arena.

Snapping out of your reverie, you notice three ghostly figures standing motionless around the plinth. Atop the plinth is a green chest.

On the plinth is a green box (closed).

You can also see a ghost on the left of the plinth, a ghost behind the plinth and a ghost on the right of the plinth here.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316c9a6290"/>
    </children>
  </item>
