    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce4ddc0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x left hand ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The ghost of a warrior stands to the left of the plinth. He brandishes a gladius, but he does not appear threatening; it is almost as if the will to fight has left him. Every do often he shakes his head and lets out a sigh.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce51160"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce51160">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to left hand ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">As you address him, the ghost looks up at you. Seemingly ashamed, he turns away. &quot;I... killed them,&quot; he says, &quot;I killed them all. I was the best gladiator in the arena. Every day they&apos;d send more fighters in to fight me, and every day I&apos;d cut them down.&quot; A tear escapes the ghostly gladiator&apos;s eye as he wails &quot;I can&apos;t do it anymore! The fight has left me! And now I must spend eternity here. Unwilling... no, UNABLE to fight. What can I do? Can you help me?&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce54c00"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce54c00">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at middle ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The ghost of a lithe gladiator armed with a net and trident skulks behind the plinth. Every so often he appears to psych himself up as if to fight, before shrinking back with a defeated look on his face.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce58180"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce58180">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to middle ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">As you address him, the ghost looks startled. &quot;Stay away from me!&quot; He yells, lifting his trident. &quot;I&apos;ll spear you! I will!&quot; After a short period of threats and posturing, the ghost crumples down, a defeated look on his face. &quot;Oh who am I kidding? I&apos;m no good at this. I don&apos;t know what I&apos;m doing. I&apos;ll never get out of this place. I just don&apos;t have the skill.&quot; A look of hopelessness crosses the ghost&apos;s face. &quot;Is there even any point in trying?&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce5be80"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce5be80">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x right hand ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">The ghost of a peasant paces back and forth angrily on the right hand side of the plinth. Every so often he will scowl at the other ghosts and mutter curses under his breath. His face is curled into a tight, angry frown.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce5f3a0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce5f3a0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to right hand ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">As you approach the ghost, lashes out at you. &quot;That&apos;s far enough! Stay back!&quot; he yells, spitting in your direction. &quot;Come for your pound of flesh have you? Come to finish me off, punish me for whatever crime you deem me guilty of this week?&quot; The ghost looks incandescent with rage as he throws invisible stones at his perceived enemies. &quot;I said GET AWAY!&quot; He lurches towards you but stops short. &quot;I&apos;m sick to death of it. I choose to live my life differently, not harming no-one, and those SHAGGERS throw me in the arena and force me to fight. Well let me tell you when I get out of here I won&apos;t stop with them. I&apos;ll put their whole family to the sword. I&apos;ll burn this whole city to the ground! I hate them all!&quot; You step away, leaving the ghost to his rage.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce626f0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce626f0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">give malachite to the left hand ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(first taking the Malachite)
The ghost takes the malachite and looks at it inquisitively. He holds it close. You can see his emotional barriers breaking down. He looks at you and very slowly starts to smile. &quot;I... I see now that I had no choice. I was a victim as much as they were. If I had not killed them I would have been killed myself. I see a long road ahead...&quot; He looks at you, a single tear rolling down his cheek as he smiles, the relief obvious in his face. &quot;But... I think I am beginning to forgive myself.&quot;

The ghost slowly begins to dissolve and rise upwards into the desert sky. Where he stood, an ornate tombstone with a roman numeral carved into it rests on the ground.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce65d10"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce65d10">
    <command xml:space="preserve">give iolite to the middle ghost</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(first taking the Iolite)
The ghost takes the iolite and looks at it inquisitively. He holds it close. You see his confidence building. &quot; you know what?&quot; he says, somewhat shakily, &quot;I don&apos;t care if I miss sometimes. If I never try then I&apos;m doomed to fail every time.&quot; The ghost slowly takes aim at some target only visible to himself. &quot;I just need a bit... more... confidence!&quot; He lets fly with his trident and cheers triumphantly. &quot;Thank you! You&apos;ve helped restore my confidence. I know I have a long journey ahead of me, but the journey of a thousand miles starts with a single step.&quot;

The ghost slowly begins to dissolve and rise upwards into the desert sky. Where he stood, an ornate tombstone with a roman numeral carved into it rests on the ground.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce69540"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce69540">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Arena of Champions
You stand inside a vast arena, and for a brief moment experience a vision of an ancient time, the stalls filled with thousands of people cheering on the mighty warriors who clashed on the sands. A rush of adrenaline fills you, the exuberance of the fight making your heart beat faster. As suddenly as it appeared, the vision fades, and the stalls lie empty, filling the arena with an unsettling silence. A plinth of alabaster occupies the centre of the arena.

On the plinth is a green box (in which are an Amethyst, a Jasper, a Ruby, an Unakite, a Rose quartz and an Obsidian).

You can also see a tombstone behind the plinth, a tombstone on the left of the plinth and a ghost on the right of the plinth here.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce6cca0"/>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce742c0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ce6cca0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">give unakite to ghost on the right</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">(first taking the Unakite)
The ghost takes the unakite and looks at it inquisitively. He holds it close. You see his anger start to fade. Slowly he sits down. &quot;I... I&apos;ve been so angry.&quot; He says, his hands shaking. &quot;So angry for so long. My rage was consuming me. But I can see now that it&apos;s holding me back. None of it has made things better... It just ate away at me, prevented me from growing.&quot; He looks up at you. &quot;Thank you. you have given me a moment of clarity, enough to see that this hatred solves nothing. I have a long way to go, and I&apos;m not sure I can forgive the people who did this to me, at least not yet; but I will no longer let their wrongs control me.&quot; The frown on the ghost&apos;s face slowly fades and is replaced by the first hint of a smile. You watch as he relaxes for the first time in a thousand years.

The ghost slowly begins to dissolve and rise upwards into the desert sky. Where he stood, a carved tombstone with a roman numeral carved into it rests on the ground.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>YES</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ce70b60"/>
    </children>
  </item>
