  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cedf210">
    <command xml:space="preserve">x stove</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A cosy wood burning stove heats the space very efficiently. You can&apos;t see where the smoke escapes to, but as the air inside the cavern is crisp and clear, you assume that the smoke must be going SOMEWHERE.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cee2710"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cee2710">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at chair</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A hand-made wooden chair, complete with plush cushions and a wonderfully soft woollen throw. You can tell from the contented look on the old man&apos;s face that the chair is exceptionally comfortable.

On the chair is The Old Man of the Mountain.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cee5d00"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cee5d00">
    <command xml:space="preserve">look at man</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">A wizened old man with a long grey beard sits on his comfy chair in front of the fireplace, gazing out contentedly at the sunset. When he notices you watching him, he smiles and says &quot;Took you long enough. I was beginning to think you weren&apos;t going to come.&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316cee9380"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316cee9380">
    <command xml:space="preserve">talk to man</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">Before you can say anything, the Old Man waves his hand and says &quot;Listen, we do not have much time. I can help you, but in exchange you must remind me of things forgotten.&quot; You stare back at him, more than a little confused. He continues, &quot;My memory is not all it once was. I was instructed to hold onto bits of information in preparation for the day you arrived, but in order to do so I needed to remove some of my own memories. Oh don&apos;t worry, I made some notes so that I could remind myself when the time came. I made three cards. Not here. In another place. You know what I mean. You&apos;ve probably already found them. On each one are clues to the memories I gave up. Well, I mean the memories are probably still in here.&quot; The old man taps the side of his head, smiling. &quot;I just need to hear a specific word to reactivate them. That&apos;s where you come in. Help me regain my memories and in return I will give you the information you need.&quot;

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
    <children>
      <child nodeId="node-0x56316ceecaa0"/>
    </children>
  </item>
  <item nodeId="node-0x56316ceecaa0">
    <command xml:space="preserve">hint</command>
    <result xml:space="preserve">That man looks kinda familiar, doesn&apos;t he? try telling him about the things he needs to remember.

&gt;</result>
    <commentary xml:space="preserve"></commentary>
    <played>NO</played>
    <changed>NO</changed>
    <temporary score="0">YES</temporary>
    <annotation xml:space="preserve"></annotation>
